WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.642 --> 00:00:18.465
It was December, and the winter was quite bad already.

2
00:00:20.006 --> 00:00:25.127
The night after Patrasche and Nello had returned from town, snow fell.

3
00:00:26.407 --> 00:00:28.588
It fell for many days after that.

4
00:00:29.892 --> 00:00:34.193
The paths in the fields disappeared, and all the streams froze.

5
00:00:37.154 --> 00:00:39.375
The sun rose late these mornings.

6
00:00:40.855 --> 00:00:43.416
Nello and Patrasche's work became harder.

7
00:00:44.897 --> 00:00:46.377
They woke up in the cold.

8
00:00:47.837 --> 00:00:50.998
They carried the milk to the silent town in darkness.

9
00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:57.504
It was hard work, especially for Patrasche.

10
00:00:57.544 --> 00:01:02.066
He was older now, and his joints were stiff and his bones often ached.

11
00:01:03.467 --> 00:01:06.208
But he would not give up his share of the work.

12
00:01:08.949 --> 00:01:13.771
Nello would have pulled the cart himself, but Patrasche would not allow it.

13
00:01:15.132 --> 00:01:18.693
Patrasche accepted only the smallest offers of help.

14
00:01:20.254 --> 00:01:24.716
Sometimes, he let Nello give the cart a push if it was stuck in the ice.

15
00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:28.241
"Take a rest today, Patrasche!"

16
00:01:29.561 --> 00:01:31.042
Nello would say in the morning.

17
00:01:31.062 --> 00:01:34.103
"I can pull the cart by myself."

18
00:01:35.524 --> 00:01:37.404
But Patrasche would not listen.

19
00:01:38.825 --> 00:01:45.027
Every day, he would bring Nello his harness; every day, he would walk steadily through the snow.

20
00:01:45.047 --> 00:01:50.590
"One must never rest until one dies," thought Patrasche.

21
00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:56.012
Sometimes, he thought that the end of his days was not far off.

22
00:01:57.428 --> 00:02:02.310
His sight was growing dim, and his bones hurt when he got up in the morning.

23
00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:11.654
"Poor Patrasche, we shall soon lie quiet together, you and I," said Jehan one night.

24
00:02:13.055 --> 00:02:19.157
He stroked Patrasche's head with his old hand, and Patrasche licked his cheek with love.

25
00:02:20.718 --> 00:02:25.760
But both of them wondered, "When we are gone, who will care for Nello?"

26
00:02:28.488 --> 00:02:33.872
One December afternoon, Patrasche and Nello were walking back from Antwerp.

27
00:02:35.793 --> 00:02:40.356
The snow had become as hard as rock over the roads and fields.

28
00:02:41.797 --> 00:02:44.719
On the road, they found a pretty little puppet.

29
00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:48.141
The puppet was beautiful.

30
00:02:49.582 --> 00:02:55.046
Its costume was made of red and gold silk, and its face was made from wood.

31
00:02:56.367 --> 00:03:00.405
Even though it lay on the road, it was clean and wasn't broken.

32
00:03:02.405 --> 00:03:05.326
Nello picked it up, thinking to find its owner.

33
00:03:06.906 --> 00:03:11.888
He stopped people passing by, but no one knew who the puppet belonged to.

34
00:03:11.908 --> 00:03:14.709
It was a busy road.

35
00:03:15.989 --> 00:03:21.290
Many merchants and farmers traveled it, and the puppet could have been lost by anyone.

36
00:03:23.191 --> 00:03:28.593
After several hours of stopping and asking people, Nello had no success.

37
00:03:30.314 --> 00:03:33.176
So he decided to give the puppet to Alois.

38
00:03:34.396 --> 00:03:37.578
He knew that she loved playing with puppets and dolls.

39
00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:46.743
Alois' father would not allow Nello to visit their house, but Nello had an idea.

40
00:03:48.124 --> 00:03:51.085
He would pass the puppet to her through her window.

41
00:03:52.466 --> 00:03:55.328
He would do it at night when nobody would see.

42
00:03:56.744 --> 00:04:01.508
He crept quietly up to the miller's house, looking carefully around.

43
00:04:03.569 --> 00:04:08.413
The light was on in Alois' room, and he tapped quietly on the glass.

44
00:04:09.934 --> 00:04:13.457
Alois opened the window and looked out, a little frightened.

45
00:04:14.998 --> 00:04:17.119
Nello put the puppet into her hands.

46
00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:21.002
"Here is a doll I found in the snow, Alois.

47
00:04:21.443 --> 00:04:23.144
Take it," he whispered.

48
00:04:25.224 --> 00:04:27.127
"I must go before anyone sees.

49
00:04:27.487 --> 00:04:29.250
Good-bye!" said Nello.

50
00:04:30.652 --> 00:04:33.976
Before Alois had time to thank him, he ran off.

51
00:04:35.418 --> 00:04:42.067
But the miller, who had heard a noise outside, opened the front door and saw Nello hurrying away

52
00:04:42.127 --> 00:04:42.728
in the dark.
